# The published list of the places an entry's program is compiled by its lemma rounds (CompilationPlaceOption): upfront, the generic entry runs the rounds and hands the executor the program they give, its one field the units it compiles (a constructor of entry_options/unit_selection); by_executor, the generic entry runs no round and hands the executor the program uncompiled, the entry's prepared compilation among the executor's inputs (gezi.contest.entry.ExecutorModuleInputs). Every entry writes one; gezi.contest.entry.Defaults.compilationPlace maps it to what the entry does.
# A Scott sum whose constructors are the tuple's fields, in the order of the
# enum's cases; an entry.lambdalattice imports this file and writes a
# constructor, and EntryData reads which alternative it takes by structure
# (gezi.contest.entry.EntryData, THE OPTIONS AS SCOTT CONSTRUCTORS).
λ export
. (λtuple. tuple λunits upfront by_executor. upfront units)
λ upfront
. (λtuple. tuple λupfront by_executor. by_executor)
λ by_executor
. export upfront by_executor
